@startuml architecture
title OAuth2 / OpenID Connect + SSO — who talks to whom
left to right direction
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam nodeFontStyle bold

actor "user / user" as human
node "Browser" as browser {
  artifact "cookies on localhost:\nAPP1_SESSION, APP2_SESSION,\nKEYCLOAK_SESSION" as cookies
}
node "Keycloak :8180\nrealm 'lesson'" as kc {
  component "login form" as login
  component "token endpoint" as token
  component "public keys (JWKS)" as jwks
}
node "app1 :8081\n(OAuth2 client)" as app1
node "app2 :8082\n(OAuth2 client)" as app2
node "ms :8083\n(resource server)" as ms

human --> browser
browser --> app1 : <b>1</b> GET /\n(no session → redirect to Keycloak)
browser --> login : <b>2</b> user/user\n→ KEYCLOAK_SESSION cookie\n→ redirect back with ?code
app1 --> token : <b>3</b> code + app1-secret\n← ID token + access token
app1 --> ms : <b>4</b> Authorization: Bearer <access token>
ms --> jwks : <b>5</b> verify token signature\n(keys fetched once)
browser --> app2 : <b>6</b> GET /\n(no session → redirect to Keycloak)
browser ..> login : <b>7</b> KEYCLOAK_SESSION already there\n→ <b>no password</b>, redirect back with ?code\n<b>= SSO</b>
app2 --> token : <b>8</b> code + app2-secret\n← ID token + access token

legend right
  through the browser (front channel): 1, 2, 6, 7
  server to server (back channel): 3, 4, 5, 8
  tokens never pass through the browser, only the one-time ?code does
endlegend
@enduml
